{{!--
Based on Tauri CLI v2.11.4 (MIT):
https://github.com/tauri-apps/tauri/blob/tauri-cli-v2.11.4/crates/tauri-bundler/src/bundle/linux/freedesktop/main.desktop
Local change (#607): Exec passes on the link a `linger://` click hands
Linger (%u), and MimeType ends in a semicolon as the spec asks. The .deb,
the .rpm and the AppImage all take their menu entry from this file.
Local change: Categories and Comment are written out, the same as the Arch
package's (packaging/arch/linger.desktop). Tauri fills them from
bundle.category, which gives one category, and bundle.shortDescription,
which falls back to the Cargo description, a developer's note. An empty
Categories fails `appstreamcli validate-tree`, and so the AppImage
catalog's test, once the AppImage carries its metainfo
(im.linger.Linger.appdata.xml).
Keep it in sync when updating the Tauri CLI.
--}}
[Desktop Entry]
Categories=Network;InstantMessaging;
Comment=A small place for friends to hang out
Exec={{exec}} %u
StartupWMClass={{exec}}
Icon={{icon}}
Name={{name}}
Terminal=false
Type=Application
{{#if mime_type}}
MimeType={{mime_type}};
{{/if}}
